From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 19:58:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: refuse TRIGGER_ACS on a radio that follows a STA

A radio with channel_follow=1 takes its channel from a STA on the same
PHY. The operator cannot apply the channel that TRIGGER_ACS reports
there, and a channel change from the STA would overlap the run. Refuse
TRIGGER_ACS on such a radio.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/hw_features.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/hw_features.c
+++ b/src/ap/hw_features.c
@@ -1467,6 +1467,8 @@ static const char * hostapd_manual_acs_r
 		return "the interface is not enabled";
 	if (iface->manual_acs_triggered)
 		return "a manual run is in progress";
+	if (iface->conf->channel_follow)
+		return "the AP follows the channel of a STA";
 	if (iface->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_ACS_OFFLOAD)
 		return "the driver offloads ACS";
 	if (hostapd_csa_in_progress(iface))
